<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Jones Group H1 pre-tax loss 2.4 mln punts.</title>
<headline>Jones Group H1 pre-tax loss 2.4 mln punts.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		18.8 loss	    vs 11.1 profit</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.40 loss	    vs 1.49 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   49.40		  vs 43.15</p>
<p> Operating result	 0.57 profit	  vs 0.97 profit</p>
<p> Exceptional		4.0 charge	   vs nil</p>
<p>Profit on sale of fixed</p>
<p>    assets		  1.36 credit	  vs 0.6 credit</p>
<p> Net interest payable   0.34		   vs 0.08</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs 0.23 charge</p>
<p> Net taxed		  2.40 loss	    vs 1.27 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - Jones Group Plc said the fall in profits arose largely from serious problems in the manufacturing division.</p>
<p>The group made a provision of four million Irish pounds to restructure the division, as indicated at its annual meeting in May. But capital profits arising from the sale of the group's premises at Beechill and the sale of a vessel reduced the impact of the provision by 1.36 million.</p>
<p>The company said that, as indicated in May, it was not paying a dividend.</p>
<p>Jones said its balance sheet remained strong with borrowings of 11.6 million punts or gearing of 44 percent.</p>
<p>The group also announced the appointment of Jim McLoughlin as finance director, effective from November 1.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
